  "steps": [
   "The scheduler starts the batch.",
   "Delete all rows of TB_R_H0253_ORDER_CONTROL_PRE (Supplier System) and insert all rows of TB_R_H0253_ORDER_CONTROL_PRE (DB Surrounding) (same columns and values). HOLD_FLAG and PO_MAPPED_FLAG are Supplier System-only columns (set in ASN Crossdock Creation): before the delete their values are kept per unique key and put back on the inserted rows; a new key gets 'N'. Cancel is not done in Supplier System: the source sends the cancelled order with ORDER_STATUS '2' (crossdock orders have '7'); Supplier System only holds, so a cancel applies to lines already on hold (HOLD_FLAG = 'Y'). Lines with status '2' are not taken by X12.",
   "No error: commit. Error: roll back step 2 (one transaction). Record the result in the Log. Exit."
  ]
